 "_about": "The hop course: a practice course for the movement, floating high in the sky away from the islands. `center` = where its middle is in the world (metres; y = the top of the start pad). `door` = the sign on the islands that takes you there (island + metres from that island's middle). `pads`: every platform in the order you hop them, `at` = [x, z] metres from `center`, `size` = [width x, depth z] in metres, `kind` start / pad / checkpoint / finish, `stage` = which part of the course. `stages`: name shown on the HUD, `speed` = the speed in Source units a second the stage is built for (400 = knife out and sprinting; 480 = the bunny-hop cap, only reached by air strafing), `strafe` = true when the stage cannot be done without air strafing (tools/course_check proves both). `fall_below` = metres under the pads at which you are put back on your last checkpoint (the clock runs on; before the first checkpoint it starts again). `thickness` = how thick a platform is. `edge_reach` = how far past a platform's edge the round body still stands (taking off) or already lands, each side, in metres (capsule radius 0.4 x sin 45 degrees): hops are measured edge to edge minus twice this.",
